<!-- 6. FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS (FAQ) -->
<section id="faq" class="py-5 bg-white">
  <div class="container py-4">
    <div class="text-center mb-5">
      <span class="badge bg-secondary bg-opacity-10 text-secondary px-3 py-2 rounded-pill fw-bold text-uppercase small mb-2">
        <i class="bi bi-question-circle me-1"></i> Help & Guidance
      </span>
      <h2 class="fw-bold text-dark mb-2">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <p class="text-muted" style="max-width: 580px; margin: 0 auto;">
        Quick answers regarding validation formats, faculty supervision capacities, and verification workflows.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-lg-8">
        <div class="accordion accordion-flush shadow-sm rounded-4 border" id="accordionFaq">
          <!-- Item 1 -->
          <div class="accordion-item rounded-top-4">
            <h2 class="accordion-header" id="faqHeading1">
              <button class="accordion-button collapsed fw-bold text-dark" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faqCollapse1">
                What are the exact Username and Register Number format rules?
              </button>
            </h2>
            <div id="faqCollapse1" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#accordionFaq">
              <div class="accordion-body text-secondary small">
                <strong>Username:</strong> Must contain purely alphabetic letters (A–Z, a–z) with a minimum length of 3 characters. Absolutely no numbers (0–9) or special characters (such as underscores, hyphens, or symbols) are permitted.<br><br>
                <strong>Register Number:</strong> Required for all Internal students. Must strictly follow the university format of <strong>2 numbers, followed by 3 letters, followed by 4 numbers</strong> (e.g. <span class="font-mono text-dark fw-bold">22BIT0061</span>).
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Item 2 -->
          <div class="accordion-item">
            <h2 class="accordion-header" id="faqHeading2">
              <button class="accordion-button collapsed fw-bold text-dark" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faqCollapse2">
                What is the difference between Internal and External students?
              </button>
            </h2>
            <div id="faqCollapse2" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#accordionFaq">
              <div class="accordion-body text-secondary small">
                <strong>Internal Students:</strong> Enrolled in on-campus university programs. They must register with an institutional email ending in <span class="font-mono">@vitstudent.ac.in</span> and supply their valid 9-character Register Number.<br><br>
                <strong>External Students:</strong> Industry or inter-university collaborators. They register with personal email addresses (e.g. Gmail, Outlook) and are strictly prohibited from using institutional VIT email domains.
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Item 3 -->
          <div class="accordion-item">
            <h2 class="accordion-header" id="faqHeading3">
              <button class="accordion-button collapsed fw-bold text-dark" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faqCollapse3">
                How does Faculty Deliverable Verification work?
              </button>
            </h2>
            <div id="faqCollapse3" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#accordionFaq">
              <div class="accordion-body text-secondary small">
                When a student submits a deliverable URL, the task transitions to <span class="badge bg-warning text-dark">IN_REVIEW</span> and an automated AI report assesses scope alignment. The assigned Faculty Guide opens the task, reviews the submission diff and AI insights, and clicks either <strong>Approve Deliverable</strong> (marking it COMPLETED) or <strong>Request Changes</strong> (returning it to IN_PROGRESS with feedback remarks).
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Item 4 -->
          <div class="accordion-item rounded-bottom-4">
            <h2 class="accordion-header" id="faqHeading4">
              <button class="accordion-button collapsed fw-bold text-dark" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faqCollapse4">
                What are the Faculty Guide team-handling capacity limits?
              </button>
            </h2>
            <div id="faqCollapse4" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#accordionFaq">
              <div class="accordion-body text-secondary small">
                Every faculty guide configures an active team-handling capacity strictly between <strong>2 and 7 concurrent teams</strong> upon registration. When a guide reaches their maximum allocated teams, student teams are automatically prevented from selecting that guide until an ongoing project finishes.
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

